== Problem Description ==
When performing a display replacement on iPhone models that require Touch IC transfer (e.g. iPhone 12-16 series), even after transferring the original touch IC from the old display to the new one, the “Unable to verify this iPhone has a genuine Apple display” message still shows up.

This usually occurs due to MTSN data mismatch — the new display doesn’t have the correct pairing data that tells the phone it’s the original display.
----

== Symptoms ==

* “Important Display Message” still shows after successful touch IC transfer.
* Everything else (touch, brightness, Face ID) may work fine.[[File:Display-message.png|thumb|"Important Display Message"]]

----

== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Confirm touch IC transfer was done properly (no bad solder joints, no missing pads).
# Connect phone to JC Programmer or equivalent tool and check if MTSN data on new display matches old display.
# If mismatch is found, message will continue to display until data is written correctly.

----

== Repair Steps ==

=== Method 1: Pre-Transfer MTSN Data ===

# Read Old Display MTSN Data:
#* Before transferring touch IC, connect old display to JC V1SE/V1SPRO  programmer.[[File:CONNCET-DISPLAY.png|center|thumb|Connect Display to Appropriate Connector]]
#* Select Read MTSN or Read Display Data and save to PC/programmer.[[File:READ.png|center|thumb|Read]]
# Write to New Display:
#* Connect new display to programmer.
#* Select Write MTSN or Write Display Data to program old display’s data to the new one. [[File:WRITE.png|center|thumb|WRITE]]
# Transfer Touch IC:
#* Once data is written, perform touch IC transfer normally.
#* Install new display → message should be gone.

----

=== Method 2: Post-Transfer Fix (If Already Transferred Touch IC) ===

# Connect Phone to Programmer:
#* After touch IC transfer, connect phone with new display installed to JC Programmer.
# Use Fix True Tone Option:
#* On JC Programmer, select Fix True Tone.[[File:TP-FIX.png|center|thumb|TP Fix]]
#* Select the appropriate display you are using, original or third party.[[File:SELECT-DISPLAY.png|center|thumb|Select Display]]
#* This will rewrite correct MTSN data to the new display flex.[[File:WRITE-COMPLETED.png|center|thumb|Verified correct data written to new display]]
# Reboot Phone:
#* Power cycle device → confirm that “Important Display Message” is cleared.